    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0478" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/8–249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-02T16:00:00+09:00">August 2, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 5—1:23 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. Information mytel 344, repeated to Canton 153 August 2, confirmed
                    officially. Informant said however this organization should not be called
                    headquarters but Gimo’s private secretariat. It is also referred to as
                    Tsungtsai’s office (office of the Director General of the Kuomintang).</p>
                <p>Sent Department 346, repeated Canton 155.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
